text:
maria: Quick sync — we want to roll out client-side header gating for the new `dynamic-batching` runtime feature. Proposal: send an `X-RW-Feature-Gates` header with comma-separated gates + `client_version` in `X-RW-Client-Version`. Canary: 5% web SDK (sticky by user id). Min supported client for gates: 1.7.0. Need guardrails (no exceptions), lightweight telemetry, and an emergency kill switch. Who can pick up parts?

ashok: sgtm. A few guardrails: SDK must ignore unknown gates (no throws), never block requests on parse errors, and provide an env var to disable sending gates (RW_DISABLE_GATES) for local/dev.

devon: I'll implement the header builder + version check in web SDK. Question: if client_version < min, do we send a header that marks `unsupported` or simply omit header and rely on server fallback? I prefer omit header so server treats it as "no gate" and falls back to stable behavior.

pri: server-side plan: if header absent or client_version unsupported -> route request to stable non-batched path and emit `gate_unavailable` metric with reason. For canary routing we'll use a hashed user_id cookie to assign buckets (sticky).

ben: putting a quick example of the client-side helper to be added to SDKs:
```js
// build headers safely
function buildGateHeaders(gates, clientVersion) {
  try {
    const gateStr = Object.entries(gates)
      .filter(([,v]) => v)
      .map(([k]) => k)
      .join(',');
    return {
      'X-RW-Feature-Gates': gateStr,
      'X-RW-Client-Version': clientVersion
    };
  } catch (e) {
    // fail-open: no header sent
    return {};
  }
}
```

dave: Telemetry: emit a tiny event `gate_eval` with fields: `gate_name`, `client_version`, `decision` (on/off/unsupported), `reason` (parse_error/min_version/assigned). Keep to <200 bytes. Also add `gate_mismatch` alert if server sees >0.5% of requests claiming a gate but server disabled it.

ashley: mobile teams: FYI android sdk 1.5.2 won't know about the header format. We'll need mobile fallback: either omit header on <1.7 or include a short flag `legacy=1` to avoid crashes. Prefer omit header.

maria: sounds good. Assignments: @devon implement header + version-check (web), @ben add gate helper & telemetry shim, @ashok add RW_DISABLE_GATES and tests + doc, @pri wire server fallback and canary bucketing, @ashley coordinate mobile opt-out plan. I'll update the rollout doc and add the canary ticket.

devon: noted — will open PR today and ping for review.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot: Canary rollout scheduled: 2026-03-18 16:00 UTC (5% web traffic). Monitor `gate_eval` and `gate_unavailable` dashboards.

ben: quick QA checklist suggestion: unit tests for unknown gate strings, e2e with server fallback, and an integration test that simulates parse error -> ensure request succeeds and no exception bubbles to user.

maria: agreed. Also adding an emergency server kill-switch: header `X-RW-Gates-Disable: 1` (server honors if present) and infra console toggle to flip gates off globally. If kill-switch used, emit high-priority alert to oncall.

pri: will add server-side detection + alert (pager) if kill-switch used more than once in a minute.

ashok: small nit — include a short README in SDK repo about header format and minimum version so integrators can adapt.

maria: thanks all. I'll draft the rollout notes and post link here once ready. :thumbsup:

devon: pinging for review when PR is up — @ben @ashok please watch for SDK tests.

ashley: will schedule a quick sync with mobile leads tomorrow to confirm opt-out approach.

maria: wrapping — target: keep canary at 5% for 48h, then 25% for 24h if no regressions, then 100% if stable. If any major regression -> immediate rollback via kill-switch.

ben: ack.
